  "change": [
    "Retain per-keyframe/yaw pose proposals for current and immediately previous seed plans, instead of requiring equality of the whole plan. Map revision/reset/lock clears proposals.",
    "Use the descriptor generator existing 1e-6 rad angular equivalence for cache lookup, including periodic wrap; do not use a fuzzy comparator in ordered containers.",
    "Every reuse evaluates current full prepared geometry and existing confidence/inlier/fitness gates. Rejected proposals retry full descriptor-seeded registration immediately.",
    "Retain finite max-iteration endpoints only as incomplete solve proposals when their numerical quality passes the existing gates. A resumed proposal must run full current registration before admission; failure falls back to the original seed in the same observation. The incomplete solve supplies no convergence or temporal evidence.",
    "Intermediate confirmation evaluates the propagated pose on current geometry; failure refines immediately; final lock requires current full converged registration plus all existing decision checks.",
    "Reuse identical geometry checks within one observation only when pose, query, target and metric agree. Explicit geometric rejection invalidates the affected seed basin; ambiguity alone does not.",
    "Split confirmation from orchestration; share observation preparation and quality evaluation. No descriptor, preprocessing, registration objective, numeric gate, input selection or tracking changes."
  ],
